  "summary_en": "Czech government plan, approved by Resolution No. 234 of 10 April 2024, for autonomous road mobility to 2025 with an outlook to 2030. It sets 13 measures across transport-technical infrastructure, legislation/standardisation/ethics, research and innovation, and public education. The aims are to enable automated vehicle operation safely and to make the Czech Republic a Central European leader.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Ministry of Transport coordinates 13 measures and reports to government by end of 2025",
   "Amend Road Traffic Act 361/2000 to permit automated vehicles, defining driver, remote operator and operational domain",
   "Support testing environments, proving grounds and pilot projects",
   "Create cybersecurity platform and certification approach for autonomous mobility, with the National Cyber Security Authority",
   "Continue work of the Ethics Commission and fund R&D (at least CZK 100 million), plus driver training and retraining"
